# L1_0 (CuAu-type) ordering target on FCC 2x2x2 = 32 atoms.
# Species: 0 = A, 1 = B; alternating (001) planes of pure A and pure B.
#
# In L1_0 each A in the z=0 layer has 4 in-plane A neighbors and
# 8 out-of-plane B neighbors (4 above, 4 below) at NN distance.
#   shell 0 (NN, z=12):  P(B|A) = 8/12 = 2/3, c_B = 0.5
#                        alpha_AB = 1 - (2/3)/0.5 = -1/3
#   shell 1 (2NN, z=6):  A's 2NN are all A (in-plane and 2 layers away
#                        the same A layer); alpha_AB = +1
#
# Same alpha signatures as L1_2 (-1/3 / +1) but on a 50:50 composition,
# which uniquely picks out the layered L1_0 ordering. The c-axis
# direction is degenerate (SCRAPS will pick one of x/y/z by chance).
SRO 0 1 0 -0.333333
SRO 0 1 1 +1.0
